  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating Decarbonization: Closing the Energy Gap through Market-Driven Solar Power Solutions (Detail Preparation Phase)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bhutan currently depends solely on glacier-fed hydropower, which generates about 99.80% of its electricity. Climate change poses a significant risk to the hydropower sector. Rapid development has significantly boosted electricity demand, and no significant hydropower capacity has been deployed recently, resulting in increased imports of carbon-intensive electricity from India. As in NDC, the recently approved 13th five-year plan set a target to materialize part of 12GW potential.Recognizing both</narrative>
  </description>
